// toolbox/segload.cla: curated Segment Loader declarations (Inside
// Macintosh II, "The Segment Loader"), SE wave 4 Task 7 -- ClarusC.APPL
// finds its own file with GetAppParms to read the runtime library out of
// its data fork (clarusc/macgui.cla's gcOpenOwnDataFork). The rest of the
// manager's trap interface comes with it, per the Toolbox-first
// principle (CLAUDE.md).
//
// Every trap word below is confirmed against Apple's own Universal
// Interfaces 3.4 (toolchain/universal/CIncludes, Retro68/
// InterfacesAndLibraries/Interfaces/AIncludes). All three have bit 11 set
// (trap & 0x0800 != 0), no `#pragma parameter` -- Toolbox (pascal)
// convention, stack arguments left to right:
//
//   GetAppParms  CIncludes/SegLoad.h:117-121: `EXTERN_API( void )
//                GetAppParms(Str255 apName, short * apRefNum, Handle *
//                apParam) ONEWORDINLINE(0xA9F5);`. Corroborated in
//                AIncludes/SegLoad.a:106 `_GetAppParms: OPWORD $A9F5`.
//                All three are fill targets, so all three are `ptr`
//                (cookbook 9(c)): apName a 256-byte Str255 buffer, apRefNum
//                a 2-byte slot, apParam a 4-byte slot (the Finder-
//                parameters handle). apRefNum is the reference number of
//                the application's open RESOURCE FILE (IM II-58; the same
//                value as CurApRefNum), not a volume or working-directory
//                refnum: to find the file's folder, pass it as ioRefNum to
//                PBGetFCBInfo (ioFCBVRefNum, ioFCBParID).
//   UnloadSeg    CIncludes/SegLoad.h:162-163: `EXTERN_API( void )
//                UnloadSeg(void * routineAddr) ONEWORDINLINE(0xA9F1);`.
//                Corroborated in AIncludes/SegLoad.a:134 `_UnloadSeg:
//                OPWORD $A9F1`.
//   ExitToShell  CIncludes/Processes.h:359-360 ("previously in
//                SegLoad.h"): `EXTERN_API( void ) ExitToShell(void)
//                ONEWORDINLINE(0xA9F4);`. Corroborated in AIncludes/
//                Processes.a:416 `_ExitToShell: OPWORD $A9F4`.
//
// Not declared: CountAppFiles/GetAppFiles/ClrAppFiles are library glue
// over the Finder-parameters handle with no trap of their own
// (SegLoad.a:58-90 is IMPORT_CFM_FUNCTION only); LoadSeg is the Segment
// Loader's own jump-table target, never called directly; Launch/Chain
// are superseded by the Process Manager's LaunchApplication.

external func GetAppParms(apName: ptr, apRefNum: ptr, apParam: ptr) = trap 0xA9F5
external func UnloadSeg(routineAddr: ptr) = trap 0xA9F1
external func ExitToShell() = trap 0xA9F4
